{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Come, all [you beasts], etc.</b> The reason is that the righteous, including the foreigners, will return, but those who burn incense to idolatry will not return. Now אָתוּ is in the imperative mood, like אִם־תְּבַעֲיוּן בְּעִיו שׁוּבוּ אָתוּ (Isaiah 21:12), meaning בֹּאוּ, derived from אָתָה מֵרִבְבוֹת קֹדֶשׁ (Deuteronomy 33:2). The meaning is that HaShem commanded the wicked nations of the world to kill the wicked of Israel, like beasts that kill one another:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {0 "Resolved the bracketed elision in the lemma head from the verse context; 'גם הגרים' rendered as 'including the foreigners.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:51.442374667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}